  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* identify the factors of the nontrivial point (w1 = 5/2 fixed; w3 drops out of rOm). Site 1 (rotRank 4): a torus-rotated vacuum f1 = s Ω_{(w1,y)} ρdiag[d1,d2,1]; the exact Solve gives its torus invariant y (compare with w2(θ12-kh)/(θ12-mh); for [3,1,0] the site-2 factor had y = w2(θ12-h)/(θ12-3h) and point A y = w2(θ12-h)/(θ12-2h)) and the torus d. Site 2 (rotRank 5, so not a rotation): same Solve (no solution expected), then span tests {e1.R.D, e1.X.R.D} for X in E12, E23, E13 and D in {1, Dy[w1], Dy[w2], Dy[w3], Dy[y-star]} with R = Rrot(z,(w1,y-star,w3)), y-star = w2(θ12-h)/(θ12-3h), plus the 3-dim span with E23^2. Orbit types of e1-descendants for reference (rotRank 4 = rotation). *)\nsolveVac2[g_, w1v_] := Module[{s}, s = Select[Quiet[Solve[Thread[(Om1[zN, {w1v, yv, 1}] . ρdiag[{d1v, d2v, 1}]) == sv g], {yv, d1v, d2v, sv}]], (sv /. #) =!= 0 &]; If[s === {}, \"none\", {yv, d1v, d2v} /. s]];\ny1P = solveVac2[f1P, wN[[1]]]; y2P = solveVac2[f2P, wN[[1]]];\nyTab = Table[{k, wN[[2]] (θ12 - hN)/(θ12 - k hN)}, {k, 1, 4}];\nystarP = wN[[2]] (θ12 - hN)/(θ12 - 3 hN);\nRstP = Normal[Rrot[zN, {wN[[1]], ystarP, wN[[3]]}]];\ndNormP = Dy[wN[[2]]]/Dy[wN[[2]]][[3]];\nf1pure = Normal[e1 . RstP . ρdiag[Dy[wN[[2]]]]];\ndTestParams = <|\"1\" -> {1, 1, 1}, \"Dy[w1]\" -> Dy[wN[[1]]], \"Dy[w2]\" -> Dy[wN[[2]]], \"Dy[w3]\" -> Dy[wN[[3]]], \"Dy[y-star]\" -> Dy[ystarP]|>;\nxOps = <|\"E12\" -> Ee[1, 2], \"E23\" -> Ee[2, 3], \"E13\" -> Ee[1, 3]|>;\nspanTab = Table[{dk, Table[With[{u = Normal[e1 . RstP . ρdiag[dTestParams[dk]]], v = Normal[e1 . xOps[xk] . RstP . ρdiag[dTestParams[dk]]]}, xk -> MatrixRank[{u, v, f2P}]], {xk, Keys[xOps]}], With[{u = Normal[e1 . RstP . ρdiag[dTestParams[dk]]]}, MatrixRank[{u, Normal[e1 . Ee[2, 3] . RstP . ρdiag[dTestParams[dk]]], Normal[e1 . Ee[2, 3] . Ee[2, 3] . RstP . ρdiag[dTestParams[dk]]], f2P}]]}, {dk, Keys[dTestParams]}];\nu0 = Normal[e1 . RstP]; v0v = Normal[e1 . Ee[2, 3] . RstP]; abF2 = LinearSolve[Transpose[{u0, v0v}], f2P];\ndescSeeds = {{\"e1\", e1}, {\"e1.E12\", e1 . Ee[1, 2]}, {\"e1.E23\", e1 . Ee[2, 3]}, {\"e1.E13\", e1 . Ee[1, 3]}, {\"e1.E12.E12\", e1 . Ee[1, 2] . Ee[1, 2]}, {\"e1.E23.E23\", e1 . Ee[2, 3] . Ee[2, 3]}, {\"e1 + e1.E23\", e1 + e1 . Ee[2, 3]}};\ndescTab = Table[{p[[1]], rotRank[Normal[p[[2]]]]}, {p, descSeeds}];\nchecks[\"site-1 factor: torus invariant y and torus (d1,d2) (w1 = 5/2)\"] = y1P;\nchecks[\"site-1 factor f1 parallel to e1.R(w1,y-star).rho(Dy[w2])\"] = (MatrixRank[{f1P, f1pure}] == 1);\nchecks[\"site-2 factor: beta/alpha in span{e1 R, e1 E23 R} (D = 1)\"] = {MatrixRank[{u0, v0v, f2P}] == 2, abF2[[2]]/abF2[[1]]};\nGrid[{{\"site 1: {y, d1, d2} of f1 = s Ω_(w1,y) ρ(d)\", y1P}, {\"y-star = w2(θ12-h)/(θ12-3h); Dy[w2]/Dy[w2][[3]]\", {ystarP, dNormP}}, {\"w2(θ12-h)/(θ12-k h), k = 1..4\", yTab}, {\"site 1: f1 parallel to e1.R(w1,y-star).ρ(Dy[w2])?\", checks[\"site-1 factor f1 parallel to e1.R(w1,y-star).rho(Dy[w2])\"]}, {\"site 2: {y, d} Solve (rotation?)\", y2P}, {\"site 2: rank{u, X u, f2} for X = E12, E23, E13 (2 = f2 in the span) and rank of the 3-dim E23 span, per D\", Column[spanTab]}, {\"site 2 = e1.(1 + b E23).R(w1,y-star), D = 1: b = β/α\", checks[\"site-2 factor: beta/alpha in span{e1 R, e1 E23 R} (D = 1)\"]}, {\"rotRank of e1-descendants\", Column[descTab]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"607004\" data-output-id=\"94\" data-out-n=\"134\" data-sub-idx=\"17\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"7\" data-sub-start=\"17\" data-sub-end=\"17\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[134]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"22\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:25.293em;vertical-align:-12.3765em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:12.9165em;\"><span style=\"top:-14.8765em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:14.8765em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:25.253em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-12.3765em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:12.8765em;\"><span style=\"top:-18.4739em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">site 1: {y, d1, d2} of f1 = s Ω_(w1,y) </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">ρ</span><span class=\"mord\">(d)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-17.2639em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:6.45em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">y-star = w2(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">12-h)/(</span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"ma