   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## §2. Undoing the rotation of the vacuum-like site, per-weight ranks, HW/LW counts (spec `site1-Qform/7-undo-site2-rotation-span.md` §1–§3, §8; globals `u15` = HW frame / point family, `u16` = lowest-weight frame)\n\nFor [3,2,0] the nontrivial point has the **roles of the two sites swapped** relative to [3,1,0]: site 1 is the (torus-rotated) vacuum $e_1^T\\rho(n)\\rho(\\Delta_{w_2})$ and site 2 is the dressed vacuum $e_1^T(1+bE_{23})\\rho(n)$, with the same $y^*=w_2(\\theta_{12}-h)/(\\theta_{12}-3h)$. Undoing the rotation therefore means: write site 1 as $s\\,e_1^T\\rho(n')$ with $n'=\\Delta^{-1}n\\Delta\\in N_+$ and move $\\rho(n')^{-1}$ onto site 2, $\\varphi=f_2\\rho(n')^{-1}$; by the flip symmetry of $V\\otimes V$ this is the spec's computation with the site labels exchanged (the covector $\\varphi$ sits at site 2, $e_1^T$ at site 1). Per-weight ranks are over the six $w_2$ below; the weight of $\\varphi$ that determines the HW state $\\nu$ is $\\nu-\\Lambda$.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* the point family at six values of w2 (w1 = 5/2, w3 = 3/5 as in P1; same (h, θ, z)): one pipeline320 run per w2. u15pt[w2] = the nontrivial point. The dressing β/α (coefficient of e1.E23.R relative to e1.R in f2) has no closed form from the pipeline; a rational fit through all data points is in the 3x3-identity cell below. *)\nu15w1 = 5/2; u15w3 = 3/5; u15w2s = {7/3, -8/9, 4/27, 3, -1/2, 11/7};\nu15ystar[w2c_] := w2c (θ12 - hN)/(θ12 - 3 hN);\n{u15t, u15runs} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[w2c -> pipeline320[zN, {u15w1, w2c, u15w3}, hN, thN], {w2c, u15w2s}]]];\nu15pt = Association[Table[w2c -> u15runs[w2c][\"points\"][[1]], {w2c, u15w2s}]];\nu15f1 = Association[Table[w2c -> Normal[u15pt[w2c][\"f1\"]], {w2c, u15w2s}]]; u15f2 = Association[Table[w2c -> Normal[u15pt[w2c][\"f2\"]], {w2c, u15w2s}]];\nu15bt = Association[Table[w2c -> With[{a = u15pt[w2c][\"dress E12,E23,E13\"][[2]]}, a[[2]]/a[[1]]], {w2c, u15w2s}]];\nchecks[\"u15 exactly one nontrivial point per w2\"] = Table[Length[u15runs[w2c][\"points\"]], {w2c, u15w2s}];\nchecks[\"u15 site-1 torus invariant y == y-star and d == Dy[w2] (normalized), all w2\"] = Table[With[{y1 = u15pt[w2c][\"y1\"][[1]]}, y1[[1]] == u15ystar[w2c] && y1[[2 ;; 3]] == (Dy[w2c]/Dy[w2c][[3]])[[1 ;; 2]]], {w2c, u15w2s}];\nchecks[\"u15 rotRank (site 1, site 2) and f1 = e1 R rho(Delta_w2), all w2\"] = Table[{u15pt[w2c][\"rotRank\"], u15pt[w2c][\"f1 = e1 R(w1,y-star) rho(Delta_w2)\"]}, {w2c, u15w2s}];\nchecks[\"u15 dressing only along E23 (E12, E13 'no')\"] = Table[u15pt[w2c][\"dress E12,E23,E13\"][[{1, 3}]], {w2c, u15w2s}];\nchecks[\"u15 beta/alpha(w2)\"] = u15bt;\nGrid[Join[{{\"w2\", \"y-star\", \"y1 (site 1)\", \"y2 (site 2)\", \"rotRank\", \"f1 = e1 R rho(Delta_w2)\", \"beta/alpha (E23)\"}}, Table[{w2c, u15ystar[w2c], u15pt[w2c][\"y1\"], u15pt[w2c][\"y2\"], u15pt[w2c][\"rotRank\"], u15pt[w2c][\"f1 = e1 R(w1,y-star) rho(Delta_w2)\"], u15bt[w2c]}, {w2c, u15w2s}], {{\"time (s)\", u15t, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
