  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (2026-10-09): [3,2,0]⊗[3,2,0], two-rotation product point and the undo\n\n**Localization (P1: h = 1/2, θ = (2/7,-3/5), z = (3/2,5/4,2/3), w = (5/2,7/3,3/5)).** At θ₁-3h the site-1 localizers are T(1,1), T(2,1), T(3,1) (matches `L2-320-localization.md`); T(2,2), T(3,2), T(3,3) vanish on ⟨Ω|; T(1,0), T(2,0), T(3,0) have rank 2 with Ω1 in their site-2 span. The joint site-2 span is 2-dimensional, {Ω1, ω₂} with ω₂ of rotRank 5 (not a rotation, not an Ω_(p,q)); the pencil Ω1+κω₂ has rotRank 5 throughout.\n\n**Product locus** (105 quadrics, exact Solve 5.5 s, 55 redundant raw components): the localizing span (site-2 factor Ω1, c(T10)=c(T20)=c(T30)=0; 53 raw components, free parameters c0, c(T11), c(T21), c(T31)) and **one isolated nontrivial point**, c = (1, T10, T11, T20, T21, T30, T31) = (81/1075, 36/215, 4/39, 1, 860/1053, -860/729, -92450/85293), the *same numbers* as the [3,1,0] point B on the common shapes. There is **no analogue of the [3,1,0] point A** (it lives on T(2,2), T(3,2), which vanish here). No continuous nontrivial component.\n\n**The roles of the two sites are swapped relative to [3,1,0]**, and the dressing is along E₂₃:\n- site 1 = e1ᵀ R(z,(w1,y*)) ρ(Δ_{w2}), Δ = diag(1/(w2-z)): a torus-rotated vacuum (rotRank 4), exact torus invariant **y* = w2(θ₁₂-h)/(θ₁₂-3h)** (= -63/43 at P1; the k = 3 member of w2(θ₁₂-h)/(θ₁₂-kh), the same y* as [3,1,0] point B), torus (2, 20/13) = Dy[w2] normalized;\n- site 2 = e1ᵀ(1 + b E₂₃) R(z,(w1,y*)) with **no** torus factor (rotRank 5, e1ᵀE₂₃ orbit type; E₁₂/E₁₃ dressings and D ∈ {Dy[w1], Dy[w2], Dy[w3], Dy[y*]} all fail); b = β/α = (6125/5676) w2/((w2-z3)(y*-z3)) at P1, w1 = 5/2 (exact rational fit through 18 points, six w2 plus twelve random; -343/484, -125/22, 125/308, -1125/2068, -375/286, ... at the six w2).\n\n**Undo.** Site 1 = s e1ᵀρ(n') with n' = Δ⁻¹nΔ ∈ N₊ exactly, so φ = f2 ρ(n')⁻¹ = (e1+bE₂₃)ρ(n n'⁻¹) sits at site 2 (flip symmetry of V⊗V). Checked exactly: ⟨f1⊗f2|HW⟩ ∝ ⟨e1⊗φ|HW⟩ on all 10 HW kets, (ρ(n')⊗ρ(n'))HW = HW. HW states: [6,4,0], [6,3,1], [6,2,2], [5,5,0], 2[5,4,1], 2[5,3,2], [4,4,2], [4,3,3] (10). The 3×3 Gauss-exponent identity (b''-a''c'')/(a''c'') = (w2-y*)/(y*-z2) holds symbolically (also symbolic z): the E13 exponent vanishes iff w2 = y*.\n\n**Per-weight ranks over six w2** ([3,2,0] has 12 weights; dim 2 at (1,2,2), (2,1,2), (2,2,1)): (a) the point as found: all full except (0,2,3), (0,3,2) ≡ 0 and (1,2,2) rank 1, i.e. 12 of 15 directions (the dressing e1ᵀ(1+bE₂₃) kills them for every w2); (b) β = 0: all full, 15/15; (c) resolvent y*, with β: as (a); (c0) resolvent y*, β = 0: the blind spot, vanishing at (0,2,3), (0,3,2), (1,1,3), (1,2,2), (1,3,1), i.e. **μ₁ ≤ 1**. This is the dual of the [3,1,0] blind spot μ₃ ≥ 2 under μ → (3-μ₃, 3-μ₂, 3-μ₁) (as [3,2,0] ≅ [3,1,0]*⊗det³), not \"μ₃ = 3\". (The \"total rank (15)\" rows of the tables are ranks of a 6×15 matrix, hence capped at 6.)\n\n**HW counts.** Fixed torus (six w2): 6 of 6 rows; fixed torus with 12 random w2: 7; **torus-completed (12 random (w2,D)): 10/10 for (a), (b), (c); 6 for (c0)** (lost: [4,3,3], [4,4,2] entirely and one direction in each of the multiplicity-2 pairs [5,3,2], [5,4,1]). LW-frame cross-check: 10/10 torus-completed, per-weight ranks full except (2,2,1) rank 1 and (2,3,0), (3,2,0) ≡ 0.\n\n**Per-irrep determination** (rank = dim at the site-2 weight ν-Λ): 9 of the 10 HW states (7 of 8 irreps) fully determined, all except **[4,4,2]**, whose site-2 weight (1,2,2) has dim 2 but rank 1 (only one linear combination of its two CG components); the LW frame does not repair it ((2,2,1) rank 1). Comparison [3,1,0]: point B 9/10 (missing the (1,1,2) direction of [4,2,2]), point A 10/10; here one family only, 9/10, with the dual pattern of missing directions. All 56 Boolean checks pass.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## §3. Avenue A2 (spec `site1-Qform/7-undo-site2-rotation-span.md` §11): the dual recipe with insertions at the site-2 points θ₂ + m h (globals prefixed `u17`)\n\nSame machinery as §1 with the roles of the two sites exchanged: M = Partition[⟨Ω⊗Ω|T_λ(x), 15] has row index = site 1 and entries over site 2; its COLUMNS (rows of Mᵀ) are the site-1 covectors. A site-2-local operator gives rank 1 with site-1 factor ∥ Ω1. The joint site-1 span replaces the site-2 span of cell 6.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* localization scan at x = θ2 + m h, m in {-1,0,1,2} and -3, all nine CBR shapes with λ1 <= 3. M = Partition[Ω2.T_λ(x), d1]: the rows of Transpose[M] are the site-1 covectors. site-2 local <=> rank 1 with the site-1 factor parallel to Ω1, i.e. Ω1 lies in the column (site-1) span. u17extra1 = 0 iff Ω1 lies in the site-1 span of M. *)\nu17ms = {-1, 0, 1, 2, -3};\nu17x[m_] := thN[[2]] + m hN;\n{u17tT, u17T} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Flatten[Table[{λ, m} -> TL2[λ, u17x[m], Zd], {m, u17ms}, {λ, shapes}]]]];\nu17M[λ_, m_] := u17M[λ, m] = Partition[Normal[Ω2 . u17T[{λ, m}]], d1];\nu17extra1[M_] := MatrixRank[Join[Transpose[M], {Ω1}]] - MatrixRank[M];\nu17tab = Flatten[Table[With[{M = u17M[λ, m]}, {m, λ, MatrixRank[M], u17extra1[M], MatrixRank[M] == 1 && u17extra1[M] == 0, Union[Flatten[M]] === {0}}], {m, u17ms}, {λ, shapes}], 1];\nu17loc = Select[u17tab, #[[5]] &][[All, {1, 2}]];\nu17zero = Select[u17tab, #[[6]] &][[All, {1, 2}]];\nchecks[\"u17 site-2 local operators (m, shape)\"] = u17loc;\nchecks[\"u17 operators with <Ω|T = 0 (m, shape)\"] = u17zero;\nGrid[Join[{{\"m (x = θ2 + m h)\", \"shape\", \"rank\", \"Ω1 outside site-1 span? (0 = inside)\", \"site-2 local\", \"<Ω|T = 0\"}}, u17tab, {{\"site-2 local\", u17loc, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"zero\", u17zero, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}, {\"time (s)\", u17tT, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"607004\" data-output-id=\"106\" data-out-n=\"271\" data-sub-idx=\"11\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"22\" data-sub-start=\"11\" data-sub-end=\"11\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[271]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:63.6401em;vertical-align:-31.55em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:32.09em;\"><span style=\"top:-34.05em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:34.05em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:63.6001em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-31.55em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:32.05em;\"><span style=\"top:-35.86em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.65em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">m (x = </span><span class=\"mord mathnormal\" style=\"margin-right:0.02778em;\">θ</span><span class=\"mord\">2 + m h)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-34.66em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.65em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"mord\">1</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-33.46em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:4.65em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord\">−</span><span class=\"m