  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result of avenue A2 (2026-10-09): the dual site-2 recipe gives NO second product point for [3,2,0]\n\n**Localization at x = θ₂ + m h** (m = -1, 0, 1, 2, -3; all nine shapes λ₁ ≤ 3; P1). Site-2 local (rank 1, site-1 factor ∥ Ω1) exactly the two expected operators: **T(1,1)(θ₂+h) = t₂(θ₂+h)** and **T(2,2)(θ₂)**. Other operators of rank ≤ 2: T(2,0)(θ₂-h) [rank 2], T(1,0)(θ₂) [2], T(3,2)(θ₂) [2]. Ω1 lies in the site-1 span of every operator with rank ≤ 2. Operators with ⟨Ω|T = 0: T(3,3)(θ₂-h) and T(2,2), T(3,2), T(3,3) at θ₂-3h. Ranks (shapes (1,0),(1,1),(2,0),(2,1),(2,2),(3,0),(3,1),(3,2),(3,3)): m=-1: 3,3,2,6,6,6,11,12,0; m=0: 2,3,6,8,1,10,12,2,4; m=1: 3,1,6,3,4,10,6,8,8; m=2: 3,3,6,8,6,10,12,12,10; m=-3: 3,3,6,8,0,10,12,0,0.\n\n**S₂ = span{1, T(2,0)(θ₂-h), T(1,0)(θ₂), T(2,2)(θ₂), T(3,2)(θ₂), T(1,1)(θ₂+h)}.** Joint site-1 span dimension 3 (Ω1, ω, ω′) at every w₂ tested; ω has **rotRank 4 (a rotation)**, ω′ has rotRank 7, and the whole pencil Ω1 + κω stays in the rotation orbit (rotRank 4 at 3 values of κ) — so the 2-plane {Ω1, ω} lies in the rotation cone, unlike the θ₁-3h case where the extra direction had rotRank 5. ω is not canonical (greedy basis mod Ω1), so its torus data are not meaningful by themselves. **Exact product locus of S₂ = only the localizing span** (3 free coefficients: 1, T(2,2)(θ₂), T(1,1)(θ₂+h); c of T(2,0)(θ₂-h), T(1,0)(θ₂), T(3,2)(θ₂) all 0); same at all six w₂.\n\n**Enlargements.** All nine shapes at θ₂+h alone (10 operators), at θ₂ alone (10), rank ≤ 4 operators at the five points (13 independent), each: exact Solve with random 3×3 compressions (every component re-verified against the uncompressed matrix): only the localizing span. All nine shapes at both θ₂ and θ₂+h (19 independent operators): the exact Solve times out, so a Groebner basis over GF(1000003) of the compressed minors (436 elements) plus the test 'c_k^j in I' shows every coefficient except 1, T(2,2)(θ₂), T(1,1)(θ₂+h) is nilpotent mod I (order ≤ 4) and the affine dimension is 3: the locus is exactly the localizing span (modular evidence, not a symbolic proof). 22 operators (adding rank ≤ 4 at m = -1, 2, -3) timed out.\n\n**Consequences.** No nontrivial point ⇒ no y-star, dressing fit, undo or per-weight ranks to compute for A2; the union with the θ₁-3h point is that point alone, so the [3,2,0] verdict stays **9/10 determined, [4,4,2] one direction short** (site weight (1,2,2): rank 1 of 2). The conjectured dual of [3,1,0]'s point A is absent in the site-2 recipe: only two localizers (T(1,1)(θ₂+h), T(2,2)(θ₂)) exist at θ₂+mh, against three at θ₁-3h, and S₂ with the extra rank-2 operators contains no product. Single-operator spans are exhausted; the next step is A3 (products of insertions at both sites).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## §13. A3 (ii) (spec `site1-Qform/7-undo-site2-rotation-span.md` §14): Q-side for [3,2,0], the minor / vacuum triple, and the pole-subset scan\n\nNew globals prefixed `u20`. Cells 2–7 run on K1 (cells 8–13 not needed here, not re-run). The Q-side is a verbatim port of the [3,1,0] notebook's cell 16 (T-polynomials in u, eigenstates of t1 + pi t2 at u = 3/7 per weight sector at 60 digits, eigenvalue polynomials, `solveQ` for direct/dual q's); it is rep-generic (uses `Λ`, `nuP`, `tL2`), so its source is read from that notebook's file and evaluated here.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Q-side port: cell 16 of L2-310-two-rotations.wb, rep-generic (Lambda, nuP, tL2, Zd all come from this notebook's cells 2-3). Same quantities: tZp, stQ, vecSt, muSt, valsSt, qdS (direct q_i), quS (dual q^j), nSt, and the Q1 checks. *)\nu20src16 = Import[\"/home/paul/git_projects/gaudin-CG/Paul/Mathematica/new-conventions/L2-310-two-rotations.wb\", \"RawJSON\"][\"cells\"][[16]][\"value\"];\n{u20tQ, u20out} = AbsoluteTiming[ToExpression[u20src16]];\nu20out",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
