   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Result (2026-10-09): A3 (ii) for $[3,2,0]$ (cells 33–41, `u20` globals)\n\n**Q-side (cells 34–35).** Port of the [3,1,0] cell 16: 225 states, all six $Q$'s found, $\\deg q^j=\\mu_j$, $\\deg q_i=6-\\mu_i$, Baxter residual $4.5\\cdot10^{-43}$, eigen-residual $4\\cdot10^{-60}$, 8 s for the whole Q-solve. Cell 35 ports cell 17 (vacuum Q's of the bra twist, 8-pole det6).\n\n**Vacuum triple (cell 36).** $\\langle\\Omega|\\psi\\rangle/\\langle x_0|\\psi\\rangle\\propto\\det_6[Q_B,Q_{vac}(w)]/\\Psi_Q$ is state independent (max $|r/r_1-1|$) only for $\\Psi_Q=\\prod_s[Q^2Q^3{-}Q^3Q^2](\\theta_s{-}3h,\\theta_s{-}4h)\\,Q^3(\\theta_s-2h)$, i.e. the triple $(\\theta-4h,\\theta-3h,\\theta-2h)$: $1.2\\cdot10^{-44}$; $(4,3,1)$: 22, $(4,2,1)$: 74, $(3,2,1)$: 86, $(4,2,0)$: 225, $(3,2,0)$: 129, $(4,1,0)$: 3175 (triples written as $(n_1,n_{21},n_{22})$ with points $\\theta-nh$). ([3,1,0] used $(4,3,1)$; the last factor moves from $\\theta-h$ to $\\theta-2h$.)\n\n**Minor (cell 37).** $\\det_2^{(0..3)}[y]/W(a,b)$ lies in span$\\{1,\\tau_{10},\\tau_{11},\\tau_{20},\\tau_{21},\\tau_{30},\\tau_{31}\\}$ ($\\tau_{22}=\\tau_{32}=\\tau_{33}=0$ exactly on the states) only for $W(3,4)$: residual $1.5\\cdot10^{-45}$; $W(2,3)$: 0.60, $W(2,4)$: 0.98, $W(3,5)$: 0.98; best other pair over all $0\\le a<b\\le5$: $(1,3)$ 0.59. Same minor as [3,1,0].\n\n**End-to-end (cell 39).** $\\Phi_P=\\sum_kc_{P,k}\\langle\\Omega|O_k$ is rank 1 (exact); $\\langle\\Phi_P|\\psi\\rangle/\\langle x_0|\\psi\\rangle\\propto\\det_6/\\Psi_Q^{(4,3,2)}\\times\\det_2^{(0..3)}[y^*]/W(3,4)$ to $1.2\\cdot10^{-44}$ over 225 states with $y^*=-63/43$ (controls: wrong $y$ 77, 1692; wrong triples 22, 74, 86).\n\n**Pole-subset scan (cells 38, 40).** All 11 subsets are in span (res $\\le5\\cdot10^{-46}$, rationalization $\\le10^{-53}$):\n\n| P | support | y-deg | y hits c_P | rank Phi generic | nonzero y with Phi rank 1 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| {0,1} | none (zero curve) | - | - | 0 | - |\n| {0,2} | T11,T31 | 2..4 | none | 1 | all y (localizing span) |\n| {0,3} | 1,T21,T30 | 3..6 | none | 2 | none |\n| {1,2} | T11,T21 | 3..4 | none | 1 | all y (localizing span) |\n| {1,3} | 1,T11,T20 | 4..6 | none | 2 | none |\n| {2,3} | 1,T10,T11 | 4..6 | none | 2 | none |\n| {0,1,2} | T11,T21,T31 | 2..4 | none | 1 | all y (localizing span) |\n| {0,1,3} | 1,T11,T20,T21,T30 | 3..6 | none | 2 | none |\n| {0,2,3} | 1,T10,T11,T21,T30,T31 | 2..6 | none | 2 | none |\n| {1,2,3} | 1,T10,T11,T20,T21 | 3..6 | none | 2 | none |\n| {0,1,2,3} | 1,T10,T11,T20,T21,T30,T31 | 2..6 | **-63/43** | 2 | only -63/43 (non-local, parallel to c_P) |\n\nThe $\\{0,1,2\\}$ curve is $(\\frac{9800}{5031}y^4,-\\frac{171500}{5031}y^3,-\\frac{12005000}{135837}y^2)$ on $(T_{11},T_{21},T_{31})$: the [3,1,0] point-A curve with the $T_{22},T_{32}$ entries (which vanish on $\\langle\\Omega|$ here) removed, hence entirely inside the localizing span, a rank-1 curve with site-2 factor $\\Omega_1$ (checked), not a new point. So **[3,2,0] has exactly one non-trivial product point (B at $y^*$, pole set $\\{0..3\\}$); the would-be point A collapses into the localizing span**, matching §10/§12 (no point A, 9/10 determined). Cells 8–13 of this notebook were not re-run (not needed for A3).",
